@style(../styles/IDocDemo.style)
@title(Units, chemistry and algorithms)

Numbers with units, chemical formulas, commutative diagrams and pseudocode.

@section(Numbers and units)

@subsection(@@num)

A number set properly: digits grouped by threes with thin spaces, a true minus, an exponent written out (6.02e23 → 6.02 × 10²³).

@num(1234567.89)

@num(6.02e23)

@subsection(@@si)

A unit set properly: upright, powers raised, thin spaces between factors; ohm, degC, micro… become their symbols.

@si(kg m s^-2)

@si(ohm)

@si(degC)

@subsection(@@qty)

A quantity: a number and its unit, never broken across a line.

@qty(9.81, m/s^2)

@qty(4.7, kohm)

@qty(25, percent)

@section(Chemistry and diagrams)

@subsection(@@ce)

A chemical formula or equation — counts lowered, charges raised, arrows: H2O, SO4^2-, Fe^3+, NaCl(aq), CuSO4*5H2O, 2H2 + O2 -> 2H2O, N2 + 3H2 <=> 2NH3 (^ a gas, v a precipitate).

@ce(2H2 + O2 -> 2H2O)

@ce(SO4^2-)

@ce(N2 + 3H2 <=> 2NH3)

@subsection(@@cd)

A commutative diagram.

@cd
A & B
C & D
A -> B : f
A -> C : g'
B -> D : h
C -> D : k
@end

@section(Pseudocode)

@subsection(@@algo)

A pseudocode algorithm listing, numbered and indented.

@algo(Binary search)
while lo <= hi
  …
@end
